<title>ITALY: Italy has non-EU trade surplus in 1996.</title>
<headline>Italy has non-EU trade surplus in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy had a cumulative 1996 non-EU trade surplus of 48.040 trillion lire in 1996 and a non-EU trade surplus of 4.390 trillion lire in December, the national statistics office ISTAT said.</p>
<p> ITALY TRADE BALANCE (NON-EU) Dec 96     Nov 96	  Dec 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	     +4.390 trln   +4.727 trln   +4.303 trln</p>
<p> Imports		     9.886 trln    10.518 trln   10.229 trln</p>
<p> Exports		    14.276 trln    15.245 trln   14.532 trln</p>
<p> Cumulative 1996	 +48.040 trln   +43.651 trln  +31.357 trln</p>
<p> Imports 1996	     125.087 trln  115.200 trln  131.368 trln</p>
<p> Exports 1996	     173.127 trln  158.851 trln  162.725 trln</p>
</text>
